{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested on exact draft 2 at 6e925763b69aa6f8496ab6b2bc7bb26e21c1050b. Design note read first in full; qualification record and both-document delta read in full.\n\nF1 (P1), partially unresolved: notes/2026-10-19-self-hosting-on-celld.md:251-269. The record now correctly includes persistent node disks, but the replacement/backup procedure still assumes SIGTERM plus process completion establishes complete handoff, then removes a VM or copies only the bucket. Pinned v0.6.2 can end a deadline-cut shutdown with exit 0 while preserving an open owner/log record, and node-log close can leave a record open/not durably sealed. A larger systemd TimeoutStopSec does not remove celld's own deadline. Thus a transient bucket outage or slow upload at shutdown still makes this procedure discard the only recoverable acknowledged tail or export an incomplete backup. This is the remaining part of the original backup/drain finding, not a demand for new infrastructure in this document-only revision.\n\nMake drain completion a checked outcome rather than an inferred successful exit. On incomplete/unknown proof, retain the VM/work directory, prevent replacement/deletion and any claim of a complete bucket-only backup, and preserve the required node data/identity. Use the upstream stopped-fleet backup contract (bucket plus node data, names, peer addresses and directories), or explicitly define a separately checked all-tail/per-cell-bucket coverage certificate before discarding node data. Quiesce application traffic/deploy writers and stop supervisors for that snapshot. H4 should include a forced slow/unavailable-bucket or unsealed-close case and show the kit refuses destructive replacement/incomplete backup, as well as happy-path restore. Update sections 4.7/5/6/9/12 consistently.\n\nPinned evidence already available locally in /private/tmp/checker-celld-design-dtwhk47a/upstream: crates/celld/main.rs:5500-5590 documents failed proof/normal recovery, deadline cutoff and exit_flushed(0); crates/celld/node_log.rs:5535-5593 leaves nonsealable or nondurable log close open; docs/guarantees.md:299-306 requires backing up bucket AND node data while preserving names/addresses/directories. Archive tag v0.6.2 SHA-256 61c073fc91b26cedc9ba042e9112750657fefee3b442f72626045b159b79b71b. Public sources: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/denoland/celld/v0.6.2/docs/guarantees.md ; https://raw.githubusercontent.com/denoland/celld/v0.6.2/crates/celld/main.rs ; https://raw.githubusercontent.com/denoland/celld/v0.6.2/crates/celld/node_log.rs . Source inspected, not executed; no claim of an independently reproduced runtime loss.\n\nF2 resolved: both notes preserve observed command-line wall times and remove the isolated bucket-cost bound, causal attribution of verify latency and measured two-node speedup. F3 resolved: optional supported APPLICATION_CONTENT/r2_buckets, bucket_name/prefix, APPLICATION_TRUST, dev-without-bucket limitation, untested package store and H4 witness are explicit. F4 resolved as design: Caddy owns and overwrites CF-Connecting-IP, loopback-only public listener prevents bypass, and forged/missing-header plus independent-client witnesses are assigned. H1 dev header remains a labelled fixture, not ingress acceptance.\n\nConclusions: runtime/coupling and bounded host-self direction remain coherent with no native judgment/entry/replay change proposed; the two-cloud kit and after-plan033 order remain appropriate; the experimental record now honestly limits timing and qualification claims. Approval remains withheld solely for F1's incomplete-drain and backup-completeness contract. H1/H2 and cloud acceptance remain future work, not completed by this review.\n\nValidation: all 2290 leaves checked, 2288 base leaves unchanged, only the two notes differ from draft 1/base. All 14 relative links and whitespace pass. Candidate tree72a317f65b65802e2162452db42afbbd60d2f161; base9554919b treebbabe9a2f6e0d374b845b46f18d9856251ed0b57; draft1 treee1b3ee9ad2f353e7cdc4b9654150dec9a4722ab4. No source/test changes, gate rerun, installs, ref mutation, push or deployment. Draft2 scratch /private/tmp/checker-celld-draft2-b7cksixd/validation.json.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2f972e09a88bcf58df21dbb078c684e335a1ae91","binding":"assigned","head":"6e925763b69aa6f8496ab6b2bc7bb26e21c1050b","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:189015d6774b946a73b5abc4d9e29c7fee3c707b\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e9e4a685a8299cb897a2ea2d41c5b4873a4b3c92\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:7a017764c36ae386816047cadbf02123b274ef2f","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}